  "world": "\u2b50\u2b50\u2b50 W-SURVIVES \u2014 THE ORDERING HOLDS WITH EVERY SIDE MATCHED. On 968 prompts fixed across every target of every curve, and with each comparison read off the curve for its OWN k pair rather than a single k=4x4 curve, both admitted objects still track the excluded object more than the label-blind arms: greedy -0.0176 against -0.1151, indep -0.0638 against -0.1212. \u2b50 The construction is validated per curve by a one-parameter model fit at j=0 alone, predicting every held-out target to 0.0100. \u26a0 AND THE MARGINS ARE MUCH SMALLER THAN EVERY EARLIER FLOOR GAVE: greedy's matched floor against the excluded object is 0.8299 and its mean matched floor against the blind arms is 0.6421, so the comparison is between two large and nearly equal nulls. \u26a0 Every floor here is a RANDOM-SUBSET floor; whether a rule-produced arm behaves like a random subset at equal overlap is not identified and needs a new selection run."
